theory_blocks.body:
A source's emission type can be identified experimentally by measuring the count rate with no absorber in place, then measuring it again after inserting each absorber in turn (paper, then a few millimetres of aluminium, then thick lead), keeping the distance and counting time fixed between readings:

- a large drop in count rate at the **paper** stage points to alpha;
- little change with paper, but a large drop at the **aluminium** stage, points to beta;
- little change with either paper or aluminium, with only a partial reduction even behind **thick lead**, points to gamma.

This is exactly the same fair-comparison skill from the previous lesson (fixed distance, fixed time), now used to compare readings across different absorbers rather than against background alone.

